cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Multi-Model Machine Learning Consensus Identifies a Dual-Interferon Gene
  Signature in Ischemic Stroke
message: >-
  If you use this software or the derived results, please cite both this
  repository and the associated paper.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Alisha
    family-names: Shamim
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
    # orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'   # TODO: add ORCID
  - given-names: Angana
    family-names: Chakroborty
    affiliation: >-
      West Bengal Education Service, Department of Higher Education,
      Government of West Bengal, Kolkata, India
    # orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'   # TODO: add ORCID
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/AliceCyrus/multimodel-consensus-stroke-scrnaseq
abstract: >-
  A multi-model consensus framework for single-cell biomarker discovery in
  ischemic stroke. Eight machine learning models spanning classical, hybrid and
  transformer-inspired architectures are trained on mouse MCAO scRNA-seq data
  (GEO GSE174574) using a strict subject-wise train/test split. Gene-level
  importance is recovered from PCA space by back-projection through the
  loadings matrix, and genes selected by at least four of six interpretable
  models are retained. The resulting 63-gene consensus signature is enriched
  for Type I and Type II interferon response genes and includes Il1rn, the
  target of the FDA-approved drug Anakinra.
keywords:
  - ischemic stroke
  - single-cell RNA sequencing
  - machine learning
  - biomarker discovery
  - consensus analysis
  - interferon signaling
  - neuroinflammation
  - transformer models
